Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About / Careers / Reloads current page: Open Rank Professor of Data Science Open Rank Professor of Data Science Full-time Southern Virginia University seeks applications for an Open Rank Professor of Data Science to begin January or August 2027. This position is intended for a data science faculty member with the breadth to teach across computer science, mathematics, and data science at the undergraduate level. Faculty in this position will typically teach four courses per semester and should be prepared to teach a variety of courses based on their expertise and the needs of the program.\r\n\r\nBecause we are a small undergraduate university, faculty in this position should be comfortable teaching a broad range of courses; over the course of a year, a faculty member may teach as many as eight different course preparations.\r\n\r\nComputer science courses may include computational data science, artificial intelligence, data structures, algorithms, databases, web development, software engineering, operating systems, and introductory programming in Python. Mathematics courses may include statistics, college algebra, trigonometry, calculus, discrete mathematics, and linear algebra. We do not expect any one candidate to be able to teach all of these courses, but we are particularly interested in candidates who can contribute across multiple areas.\r\n\r\nAs a faith-based university, Southern Virginia University seeks faculty who support and contribute to its mission and values.\r\n\r\nThe position is open rank and may be filled at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor level, depending on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Responsibilities Teach four undergraduate courses per semester across computer science, mathematics, and data science Develop and refine course material Advise and mentor students Fulfill faculty service assignments Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Mathematics, or a related field Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate courses in multiple areas of computer science, mathematics, and/or data science Strong communication skills and a love of teaching Preferred Qualifications PhD in Data Science, Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field Experience teaching a range of undergraduate courses across computer science, mathematics, and/or data science Industry experience as a data scientist or software engineer, or experience as a computational researcher Experience developing courses and mentoring undergraduate students Applications Applications should include a CV, a letter of interest addressing the desired qualifications, the university’s mission, and evidence of teaching effectiveness, and a list of 3 professional references. These materials should be sent as a single PDF to Opens email to Provost provost@svu.edu . A sample of research may also be included in a separate PDF. About Southern Virginia University Southern Virginia University is a private, faith-based institution of higher education aligned with the restored gospel of Jesus Christ as taught by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. As a university, we gather faithful Latter-day Saints and those who share our values, lift intellectually, socially, and spiritually, and launch into successful lives and careers. Applicants are invited to learn more about the university at svu.edu/mission . Gather. Lift. Launch. Subscribe to our Newsletter About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy