    "https://svu.edu/about/careers/assistant-director-of-admissions/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Admissions - Southern Virginia University Skip to content Apply Now Request Info Cancel Search for: About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern Quick Links: my svu News Calendar & Events Alumni Contact Us Knight Athletics Careers Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About About SVU Our Mission → Our Mission Why We Gather How We Lift Prepare to Launch Faith → Faith in Jesus Christ YSA Stake & Wards Alignment with the Restored Church Code of Conduct Missionaries Institute of Religion News Academics Academics at SVU Faculty Office of the Provost Majors, Minors, & Programs → Majors & Minors Career Concentrations Professional Tracks Honors Program Academic Resources → Catalog Canvas Login Academic Calendar Library Academic Support Services SVU Online Bookstore Career Services Admissions How to Apply Tuition & Affordability Visit Campus Orientation Admissions Team Financial Aid Financial Aid 101 Types of Aid Scholarships & Grants Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Team Financial Wellness Resources Student Life Knight Life Get Involved → Athletics Arts Esports Music Program Student Leadership & Clubs Housing Dining Campus Student Support Services Student Life Team Giving Give to SVU Giving Campaigns Ways to Give Join a Giving Society Our Advancement Team Quick Links: my svu News Calendar & Events Alumni Contact Us Knight Athletics Careers Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About / Careers / Reloads current page: Assistant Director of Admissions Assistant Director of Admissions Full-time Southern Virginia University seeks a strategic, mission-driven Assistant Director of Admissions to lead and support enrollment marketing initiatives, CRM management, and prospective student engagement strategies. This position plays a critical role in shaping the student recruitment funnel by combining data-informed marketing, communication strategy, and relationship-centered admissions practices.\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate is both analytically minded and highly relational, with experience in enrollment marketing, customer relationship management (CRM) systems, digital communications, and admissions operations. This individual will help strengthen the university’s mission by developing systems and campaigns that connect prospective students to a faith-centered educational experience aligned with the values of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Responsibilities Develop and execute strategic communication plans designed to increase inquiries, applications, campus visits, and enrollment conversion. Manage prospective student communication flows across email, text, phone, print, and digital platforms. Collaborate with marketing and admissions teams to create compelling enrollment content and recruitment campaigns. Assist in the development of digital marketing strategies, including lead generation, social media engagement, and campaign tracking. Analyze recruitment and marketing performance metrics to improve engagement and conversion outcomes. Support branding and messaging efforts that communicate Southern Virginia University’s mission, culture, and student experience. Serve as a primary administrator and strategist for the admissions CRM system. Build and maintain communication workflows, automations, dashboards, reports, and recruitment pipelines. Ensure data integrity, segmentation accuracy, and efficient prospect management processes. Develop reporting tools and enrollment analytics to support admissions decision-making and recruitment forecasting. Train admissions staff on CRM best practices and communication standards. Coordinate CRM integrations and liaise with IT to support process improvements across admissions operations. Recruit and counsel prospective students and families throughout the admissions process. Assist with recruitment territory management and admissions events as needed. Support campus visit experiences, admitted student programs, and enrollment initiatives. Represent the university at recruitment events, conferences, and community outreach activities. Supervise student workers or admissions staff as assigned. Contribute to departmental planning, enrollment strategy development, and annual recruitment goals. Strategic thinking with strong attention to detail. Ability to interpret enrollment data and translate insights into actionable strategies. Strong relationship-building and collaborative leadership skills. Proficiency in CRM systems, Excel/reporting tools, and communication platforms. Ability to balance mission-centered recruitment with data-informed enrollment practices. Professional presentation and public speaking skills. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Experience in admissions, enrollment marketing, CRM management, higher education marketing, or related fields. Strong understanding of CRM systems, marketing automation, and data-driven communication strategies. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational, analytical, and project management abilities. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to the mission and values of Southern Virginia University. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends and travel as needed. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Experience with Slate, Salesforce, Element451, HubSpot, or similar CRM/enrollment platforms. Familiarity with digital advertising, lead nurturing, and enrollment funnel analytics. Applications Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to Human Resources at hr@svu.edu . Applications will be accepted and reviewed until the position is\r\nfilled. About Southern Virginia University Southern Virginia University is a private, faith-based institution of higher education aligned with the restored gospel of Jesus Christ as taught by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. As a university, we gather faithful Latter-day Saints and those who share our values, lift intellectually, socially, and spiritually, and launch into successful lives and careers. Applicants are invited to learn more about the university at svu.edu/mission . Gather. Lift. Launch. Subscribe to our Newsletter About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern New Tab, Instagram New Tab, Facebook New Tab, Youtube New Tab, LinkedIn ©2026 Southern Virginia University  • phone link 540-261-8400 •  1 University Hill Drive, Buena Vista, VA 24416  • link Privacy Policy"
