    "https://svu.edu/about/careers/assistant-softball-coach/": {
      "title": "Assistant Softball Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Softball Coach - Southern Virginia University Skip to content Apply Now Request Info Cancel Search for: About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern Quick Links: my svu News Calendar & Events Alumni Contact Us Knight Athletics Careers Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About About SVU Our Mission → Our Mission Why We Gather How We Lift Prepare to Launch Faith → Faith in Jesus Christ YSA Stake & Wards Alignment with the Restored Church Code of Conduct Missionaries Institute of Religion News Academics Academics at SVU Faculty Office of the Provost Majors, Minors, & Programs → Majors & Minors Career Concentrations Professional Tracks Honors Program Academic Resources → Catalog Canvas Login Academic Calendar Library Academic Support Services SVU Online Bookstore Career Services Admissions How to Apply Tuition & Affordability Visit Campus Orientation Admissions Team Financial Aid Financial Aid 101 Types of Aid Scholarships & Grants Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Team Financial Wellness Resources Student Life Knight Life Get Involved → Athletics Arts Esports Music Program Student Leadership & Clubs Housing Dining Campus Student Support Services Student Life Team Giving Give to SVU Giving Campaigns Ways to Give Join a Giving Society Our Advancement Team Quick Links: my svu News Calendar & Events Alumni Contact Us Knight Athletics Careers Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About / Careers / Reloads current page: Assistant Softball Coach Assistant Softball Coach Part-time Southern Virginia University (SVU) is seeking an Assistant Softball Coach. The Assistant Softball Coach will assist in recruiting and coaching student-athletes, reports to the Head Softball Coach, and supports the SVU mission as well as the ideals of the USA South Conference and the NCAA Division III athletic philosophy. Responsibilities Coaching Assist in developing practice plans for the team, including infield/outfield, hitting, pitching, and catching. Assist with game planning and strategies. Assist, as needed, with securing travel arrangements and meals. Maintain a positive relationship with student-athletes as they graduate and become alumni. Recruiting In coordination with the Head Coach, recruit potential student-athletes who align with the Softball program and SVU ideals. Identify and recruit individuals who are competitive and demonstrate the potential to contribute to the program. Regularly communicate with recruits throughout the recruiting process. Attend recruiting events and venues to evaluate potential student-athletes. Host recruits on campus and assist with their campus visit experience. Help student-athletes transition into the university and Softball program. Administration Attend weekly coaching meetings and regular athletic staff meetings. Provide input regarding program direction and needs. Assist with administrative tasks as requested by the Head Coach and/or Athletic Department staff. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution of higher education or equivalent experience. Proven Coaching ability Experience recruiting/retaining students in athletic and/or academic program settings Strong knowledge of NCAA Softball rules. Willingness to work non-traditional hours, including evenings, weekends and holidays Ability to operate a vehicle according to federal and state laws/regulations Ability to work both independently and with a team committed toward Student-Athlete well-being Good communication skills Some overnight travel Ability to plan and conduct softball camps, clinics and leagues, in coordination with the Head Coach Preferred Qualifications Experience with coaching pitchers at the elite club and/or collegiate level 2 years playing or coaching at the collegiate level Applications Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to Human Resources at hr@svu.edu . Applications will be accepted and reviewed beginning June 9 until the position is\r\nfilled. About Southern Virginia University Southern Virginia University is a private, faith-based institution of higher education aligned with the restored gospel of Jesus Christ as taught by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. As a university, we gather faithful Latter-day Saints and those who share our values, lift intellectually, socially, and spiritually, and launch into successful lives and careers. Applicants are invited to learn more about the university at svu.edu/mission . Gather. Lift. Launch. Subscribe to our Newsletter About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern New Tab, Instagram New Tab, Facebook New Tab, Youtube New Tab, LinkedIn ©2026 Southern Virginia University  • phone link 540-261-8400 •  1 University Hill Drive, Buena Vista, VA 24416  • link Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://svu.edu/about/careers/associate-registrar/": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Associate Registrar - Southern Virginia University Skip to content Apply Now Request Info Cancel Search for: About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern Quick Links: my svu News Calendar & Events Alumni Contact Us Knight Athletics Careers Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About About SVU Our Mission → Our Mission Why We Gather How We Lift Prepare to Launch Faith → Faith in Jesus Christ YSA Stake & Wards Alignment with the Restored Church Code of Conduct Missionaries Institute of Religion News Academics Academics at SVU Faculty Office of the Provost Majors, Minors, & Programs → Majors & Minors Career Concentrations Professional Tracks Honors Program Academic Resources → Catalog Canvas Login Academic Calendar Library Academic Support Services SVU Online Bookstore Career Services Admissions How to Apply Tuition & Affordability Visit Campus Orientation Admissions Team Financial Aid Financial Aid 101 Types of Aid Scholarships & Grants Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Team Financial Wellness Resources Student Life Knight Life Get Involved → Athletics Arts Esports Music Program Student Leadership & Clubs Housing Dining Campus Student Support Services Student Life Team Giving Give to SVU Giving Campaigns Ways to Give Join a Giving Society Our Advancement Team Quick Links: my svu News Calendar & Events Alumni Contact Us Knight Athletics Careers Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services About / Careers / Reloads current page: Associate Registrar Associate Registrar Full-time Under the general direction of the University Registrar, the Associate Registrar provides leadership in the daily operations of the Registrar's Office, with primary responsibility for ensuring the university's compliance with state and federal reporting requirements, including IPEDS, SCHEV, and the National Student Clearinghouse (NSC). This position plays a key role in maintaining the accuracy, integrity, and timeliness of institutional data submitted to external agencies. Responsibilities Serves as one of the university’s primary points of contact for the Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS) reporting, ensuring accurate and timely submission of all required surveys Prepares and submits required enrollment and degree reports to the State Council of Higher Education for Virginia (SCHEV), ensuring compliance with state reporting standards and deadlines Manages enrollment and degree reporting to the National Student Clearinghouse (NSC) Monitors changes to state and federal reporting requirements and updates internal processes and procedures accordingly Collaborates with other administrative offices to ensure compliance and consistency of data across all external reports Assists the Registrar in the daily management and operation of the Registrar’s Office Oversees the maintenance of student records in the Jenzabar system, a variety of software, and hard-copy files, in accordance with FERPA and university confidentiality policies Interprets and applies academic policies and procedures, advising staff, faculty, and students on how requirements apply to individual academic situations Assists in the evaluation of transfer and prospective student transcripts Assists in the coordination of registration, grading, and academic record processes each term Supports commencement and graduation processes, including degree audits and certification of candidates for graduation Provides backup support for Veterans’ Administration (VA) education benefits certification and reporting Assists in training, guiding, and supporting Registrar’s Office staff on reporting procedures and best practices Leads and serves the University and staff by example in supporting the mission, rules, and policies of the University, as well as through strong work ethic and overall job performance Performs other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required Minimum of 2–3 years of experience in a Registrar’s Office or related higher education administrative role, with direct experience in state and/or federal compliance reporting strongly preferred Demonstrated understanding of FERPA and other regulations governing student records Strong analytical skills with high attention to detail and accuracy in data management and reporting Ability to interpret and communicate complex policies and regulatory requirements clearly to a variety of audiences Demonstrated ability to use and learn new software programs (knowledge of Jenzabar preferred) Strong oral and written communication skills Ability to manage multiple deadlines and prioritize effectively in a fast-paced office environment Applications Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to Human Resources at hr@svu.edu . Applications will be accepted and reviewed until the position is\r\nfilled. About Southern Virginia University Southern Virginia University is a private, faith-based institution of higher education aligned with the restored gospel of Jesus Christ as taught by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. As a university, we gather faithful Latter-day Saints and those who share our values, lift intellectually, socially, and spiritually, and launch into successful lives and careers. Applicants are invited to learn more about the university at svu.edu/mission . Gather. Lift. Launch. Subscribe to our Newsletter About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern New Tab, Instagram New Tab, Facebook New Tab, Youtube New Tab, LinkedIn ©2026 Southern Virginia University  • phone link 540-261-8400 •  1 University Hill Drive, Buena Vista, VA 24416  • link Privacy Policy"
