d written communication skills Excellent judgment and decision-making abilities Proven work ethic and self-motivation Ability to work with diverse personalities and perspectives Bachelor’s Degree or at least three years of relevant work experience Preferred Qualifications Background in college financial aid At least 3 years of work experience in financial services, customer service, sales, or a related field Experience with Jenzabar or similar student information system (SIS) software Master’s Degree Applications This is a part-time hourly position. Occasional overtime or weekend work may be required during peak financial aid processing periods.\r\n\r\nInterested applicants should submit a resume and cover letter to hr@svu.edu . The position will be open until filled. About Southern Virginia University Southern Virginia University is a private, faith-based institution of higher education aligned with the restored gospel of Jesus Christ as taught by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. As a university, we gather faithful Latter-day Saints and those who share our values, lift intellectually, socially, and spiritually, and launch into successful lives and careers. Applicants are invited to learn more about the university at svu.edu/mission . Gather. Lift. Launch. Subscribe to our Newsletter About Our Mission Faith in Jesus Christ Careers News Blog Admissions How to Apply Affordability Scholarships & Grants Visit Campus Links Knight Athletics Bookstore Canvas Catalog Library Knight App Make a Payment my svu Resources Accreditation Alumni Apparel & Gifts Brand Guidelines & Logos Calendar Campus Map Request Transcripts Transportation Services Help Contact Us / Directory Accessibility Statement Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Campus Map Title IX Safety & Security Reports Report a Concern New Tab, Instagram New Tab, Facebook New Tab, Youtube New Tab, LinkedIn ©2026 Southern Virginia University  • phone link 540-261-8400 •  1 University Hill Drive, Buena Vista, VA 2